WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:03.980
I'm going to have Midorin 
work here from now on.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:06.730
Basically, you're fired!

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:10.820
Actually...

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:12.250
I've never needed you at all.

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:16.490
Very well.

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:17.120
Huh?

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.490
Thank you for everything.

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:57.800
<b>Episode 7:  My Maid Doesn't Come Anymore</b>

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:05.020
She accepted that quite readily.

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:08.100
Now I feel like the bad person here.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:09.210
Well, of course you are.

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:14.200
Normally, you'd notify someone that they're 
being let go a month ahead of time.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.690
The Labor Standards Act sets 
forth certain stipulations.

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:18.150
Tell me that first!

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:21.900
Well, if she has no problem with it,
I doubt it'll be an issue.

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:24.840
Milady!

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:26.210
Stop being so annoying!

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:30.040
<i>I guess she really wasn't 
that serious after all.</i>

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:31.910
Well, whatever.

00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:35.550
Oh, but she might try to spy on us for a bit.

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:37.340
I'm going to have you work 
here for a little bit

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:38.470
just to camouflage what we're really doing.

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:39.160
Right.

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:41.160
Anyway, make me some dinner.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:42.180
I'm hungry.

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:43.550
Leave it to me!

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:47.040
What is this?!

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:47.950
Vomit?!

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:48.600
It's curry.

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:51.520
The ingredients to make 
curry were already there.

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:55.800
In any event, I'm going out to
 buy things for dinner.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.230
Please watch the house for me.

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:59.820
<i>She had curry planned for me tonight...</i>

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:05.260
Maybe it just looks bad.
I'm sure it won't taste that...

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:09.370
No, it tastes like vomit, too.

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:15.020
It's Midorin's special curry:
a curry that mimics real vomit.

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:16.880
Why are you making weird 
philosophical curries?

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:18.520
Are you disappointed?

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:20.260
I guess you could say I've lost all hope.

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:24.050
Yes, those are exactly the 
words I was looking for.

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:25.000
I forgot!

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.260
Midorin is a huge masochist!

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:27.830
Make food properly!

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:29.330
This is your job, you know?

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:31.200
You're wasting food!

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:32.270
<b>Squee</b>

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:32.930
An elementary schooler is yelling at me!

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:34.520
Everything's a pain with you.

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:36.020
Don't worry about anything.

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:39.100
I'll take responsibility and eat it all.

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:42.150
Th-This is bad.

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:43.160
Jeez!

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:46.940
Yes, this is how it felt...

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:48.800
That look of disappointment 
on everyone's face,

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:50.430
and a taste so bad that your 
stomach would just reject it.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:55.610
This is the feeling that got me addicted 
to, and good at making, bad food.

00:03:57.320 --> 00:04:00.220
I wonder if I could even make 
something that tasted good...

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:02.060
Well, just try!

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:02.930
I'll do what I can.

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:07.550
In any event, I'll get some top-shelf 
sushi with the pocket money I have on me.

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:09.240
<i>This maid didn't even have 
a job until a moment ago.</i>

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:10.880
<i>How much "pocket money" could she have?</i>

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:12.110
Oh, hello.

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:13.560
I'd like to place an order.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:24.070
I'm home.

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:26.180
Yasuhiro, I, uh...

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:29.640
I got an email about our maid, if 
that's what you want to talk about.

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:32.050
She told me not to get mad at you.

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:37.980
But I mean the situation's really unfortunate.
Her food was really great.

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:40.120
It was always good.

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:42.840
The new maid cooked for you today, right?

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:45.360
There's some good sushi over there.

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:47.860
She made it?

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:53.760
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:57.050
<i>I should feel a lot better 
now that she's gone,</i>

00:04:57.050 --> 00:04:59.600
<i>but instead now I just 
don't know how to feel.</i>

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:01.730
<i>It's like I'm the one 
who did something wrong.</i>

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:05.050
<i>She did all sorts of things 
to me I didn't like, too.</i>

00:05:05.050 --> 00:05:06.240
<i>It's only fair.</i>

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:10.740
Milady, I'm really sorry.

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:13.920
I-I'm not apologizing!

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:19.500
<b>Vienna Sausages | White Rice | Pickled Asian Radish | Tuna</b>

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:20.670
What's this about?

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:21.710
It's breakfast.

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:23.710
It doesn't taste great, but it'll 
get you the calories you need.

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:25.010
I want something that tastes good, too!

00:05:25.770 --> 00:05:28.120
Actually, where's Yasuhiro?

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:29.690
It sounds like he has a meeting today.

00:05:29.690 --> 00:05:30.890
He left without eating.

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:36.640
You could just have toasted some bread.

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:37.560
I did.

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:38.270
Huh?

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:45.170
I could only watch the 
bread as it kept burning...

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:50.530
<i>It's burning...</i>

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:54.290
<i>I could open the door and save it!</i>

00:05:54.550 --> 00:05:56.860
<i>Am I just going to sit here and do nothing?!</i>

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:00.050
The guilt was overwhelming.

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:01.670
I think you should see a shrink.

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:05.340
This was a lot of effort for me,

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:09.010
but in the end, my body just 
wants to make bad food.

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:12.690
This tastes terrible.

00:06:12.690 --> 00:06:17.300
But you said that woman's food was good 
and that you want to eat it again.

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:20.660
I still like to eat good-tasting food.

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:21.940
Well, this is an issue.

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:24.020
Which is why I have provided pre-made food.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:26.530
Then at least buy pre-made 
stuff that tastes good!

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:33.440
Misha-chan, are you feeling sick?

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:35.370
I think I'm getting a stomachache...

00:06:36.230 --> 00:06:38.890
Well, that's just pathetic.

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:40.170
Morikawa-san!

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:43.980
I licked up the curry I had leftover 
from last night this morning.

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:45.340
Why are you trying to brag about that?

00:06:45.620 --> 00:06:49.000
I guess really pretty girls 
get sick really easily.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:51.550
Well, she was out sick for a long time.

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:56.350
Yui's stomach's starting to hurt, too...

00:06:56.660 --> 00:06:57.310
Peek.

00:06:57.560 --> 00:06:59.560
Maybe the curry went bad.

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:02.150
There's a lot of parasites going around.

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:04.940
You're treating me completely differently!

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:13.170
I'm tired...

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:14.080
I'm back—

00:07:22.760 --> 00:07:23.540
You're home, huh?

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:25.040
It's spotless.

00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:27.420
I know, right?

00:07:27.850 --> 00:07:30.040
I learned how to clean and do the 
laundry while with the force.

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:32.140
Then why can't you cook?

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:34.680
It's the supply staff's 
job to provide the food.

00:07:35.060 --> 00:07:36.220
But do not fret.

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:36.810
Hmm?

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:41.310
Our dessert today is a cake 
made by a professional.

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:43.190
Yay!

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:48.320
<i>Well, I guess we didn't 
need that woman after all.</i>

00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:50.470
Hmm?

00:07:51.560 --> 00:07:53.220
Where did you get this cake?

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:54.860
A cake shop near the station.

00:07:54.860 --> 00:07:56.670
I heard it was the best in this area.

00:07:56.670 --> 00:07:58.490
Yeah, that place is popular.

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:00.420
<i>Was this is how it tasted?</i>

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:02.000
<i>I think that woman makes it better—</i>

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:05.280
<i>No, this is just fine!</i>

00:08:06.620 --> 00:08:08.090
Oh, yeah...

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:08.500
Hmm?

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:10.440
Pick what you want to eat tonight.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:11.260
Have a hand-rolled sushi party with your family!!

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:11.260
<b>Fall Season
Cheese Festival</b>

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:11.260
<b>Coupon</b>

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:11.260
Wow!

00:08:11.660 --> 00:08:13.400
Then I want pizza!

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:15.070
The one with cheese in the crust!

00:08:15.070 --> 00:08:16.260
No problem.

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:18.390
<b>One Week Later</b>

00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:25.480
I keep eating pizza and sushi everyday...

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:26.900
I'd like to go back to eating normally...

00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:38.280
Hmm?

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:40.550
Midorin?

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:42.320
What's wrong?

00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:43.290
What are you looking—

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:55.130
Wh— Wh-Wh-Wh-What should I do?!

00:08:55.130 --> 00:08:55.840
Huh?

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:57.490
Kamoi is standing next to a river!

00:08:57.490 --> 00:08:58.590
What a beautiful sight!

00:08:58.590 --> 00:09:00.950
Right. I don't really get it.

00:09:00.950 --> 00:09:01.860
Why don't you try saying something?

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:03.260
I-I can't!

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:06.120
I ain't prepared ta do somethin' like that!

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:08.760
Why are you talking like that?

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:11.280
Ya go fer me!

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:12.780
Huh? Wait—

00:09:17.350 --> 00:09:18.880
Ow...

00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:20.160
Jeez...

00:09:23.720 --> 00:09:25.790
It's been a while, Milady.

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:27.810
No, I should say "Misha-san."

00:09:30.650 --> 00:09:32.170
What are you talking about?

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:35.630
You wouldn't leave me alone, and now...

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:39.560
You're the one who rejected me.

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:44.410
I am someone you do not need in your life.

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:45.940
That's all there is to it.

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:47.660
Someone that I don't need?

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:49.440
I don't really feel that strongly...

00:09:49.740 --> 00:09:54.940
There were a few... minor things... 
that you did help me with.

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:56.430
For example...

00:09:58.620 --> 00:10:01.210
Food?

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:05.970
I apologize for firing you,

00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:07.210
so please...

00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:09.960
I want you to make me food and snacks again!

00:10:12.980 --> 00:10:13.840
Huh?

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:15.260
I got that on film!

00:10:16.070 --> 00:10:17.550
You can't go back on your word now!

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:18.220
What?!

00:10:18.940 --> 00:10:21.880
Ukai-san's cooking is atrocious.

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:24.970
I knew that, sooner or 
later, this would happen.

00:10:25.690 --> 00:10:27.230
My strategy succeeded!

00:10:27.510 --> 00:10:28.420
Hey!

00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:29.860
So you were planning this from the beginning?

00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:30.730
That's right.

00:10:34.580 --> 00:10:36.960
I really hate you, you know that?!

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:40.110
I want you to make me food and snacks again!

00:10:40.900 --> 00:10:42.620
I hate you,

00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:45.370
but I do like your food.

00:10:47.310 --> 00:10:52.000
<i>Winning over someone's stomach 
is always the best tactic.</i>

00:10:55.110 --> 00:10:58.140
Kamoi Tsubame will return to her post!

00:10:58.140 --> 00:10:59.920
Hold on a second!

00:11:01.370 --> 00:11:02.640
What are you going to do with me?

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:04.080
Oh, I forgot.

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:05.260
<b>Heart skip</b>

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:05.260
She forgot me!

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:08.000
Wait, no. If you're going to fire me,

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:10.390
then you need to notify 
me a month beforehand.

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:11.260
In other words...

00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:15.190
Everything will be solved if you allow 
Kamoi and I to work simultaneously.

00:11:15.570 --> 00:11:17.320
O-Okay.

00:11:17.780 --> 00:11:20.320
<i>I don't know if Yasuhiro 
has that much money...</i>

00:11:21.620 --> 00:11:24.250
Well, I can stomach it for a month.

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:27.660
However, do not get in my way.

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:29.540
I'll be a good girl.

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:31.350
<i>Will this even work?</i>

00:11:31.350 --> 00:11:32.040
<i>But...</i>

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:34.780
<i>I'm looking forward to dinner tonight.</i>

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:41.050
<b>Uzamaid!</b>

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:46.050
<b>Uzamaid!</b>

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:55.610
Good morning.

00:11:56.450 --> 00:11:57.810
Oh, Kamoi.

00:11:57.810 --> 00:11:58.820
I've been waiting for you.

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:00.420
Since when?

00:12:00.420 --> 00:12:04.000
I've been waiting since last 
night to ensure I was not late.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:07.140
It's only October, but it sure 
freezes you to the bone at night.

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:11.540
The neighbors will see you,
so just come at a normal time.

00:12:11.890 --> 00:12:15.440
That woman has been crouched down in 
front of that house since last night.

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:17.870
Was she locked out? I feel bad for her.

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:20.010
They both aren't the wife, right?

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:21.720
I can't really hear them,

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:23.690
but I know they're looking 
at me like I'm trash.

00:12:23.690 --> 00:12:25.460
I'm a crazy masochist, so it's 
making me shake with pleasure.

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:26.990
You just caught cold.

00:12:26.990 --> 00:12:28.890
In any event, let's get inside.

00:12:30.200 --> 00:12:33.600
The two of them always wake up around 7.

00:12:33.930 --> 00:12:36.410
So we make breakfast in that time.

00:12:36.410 --> 00:12:38.110
We don't even have 30 minutes left.

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:40.600
That's...

00:12:40.600 --> 00:12:42.100
More than enough time!

00:12:47.040 --> 00:12:48.130
Everything's finished.

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:51.180
That was wonderful work.

00:12:51.180 --> 00:12:52.810
I was so taken aback, I couldn't even move.

00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:54.410
Yeah, and it's probably better that way.

00:12:54.410 --> 00:12:58.420
<b>Squid Shiokara</b>

00:12:54.410 --> 00:12:58.420
<b>Fresh Sea Cucumbers</b>

00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:58.920
At least allow me to add this shiokara
and sea cucumber as a topping!

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:00.800
Put that on your own portion.

00:13:01.230 --> 00:13:05.380
In any event, I need to handle the most 
important assignment this morning.

00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:07.650
First Lieutenant, don't do 
anything you don't need to,

00:13:07.650 --> 00:13:10.140
and just get some coffee ready.

00:13:10.530 --> 00:13:12.140
The most important assignment?

00:13:12.580 --> 00:13:15.060
Waking up Milady, obviously.

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:18.870
I enter her room five minutes 
before she's to wake,

00:13:18.870 --> 00:13:21.820
take pleasure in watching her sleep, 
and then gently wake her up.

00:13:22.770 --> 00:13:24.570
It's something that gives me a 
little comfort every morning!

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:27.650
Good morning.

00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:30.240
Why?!

00:13:30.550 --> 00:13:32.620
It's always so freaky how 
you try to wake me up.

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:37.900
So I woke up earlier than 
when you normally come.

00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:40.850
But you never can wake up 
by yourself, and yet...

00:13:40.850 --> 00:13:45.560
I realized that it'd feel much better waking
up on my own than waking up with you there.

00:13:46.040 --> 00:13:47.510
Good morning.

00:13:48.050 --> 00:13:51.660
It's rather lively with 
three women around now—

00:13:56.020 --> 00:13:57.270
Uh...

00:13:57.810 --> 00:13:59.770
Maybe I'll start on my breakfast.

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:02.770
Time to eat.

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:09.250
<i>Handmade bread with tons of butter.</i>

00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:10.780
<i>This is good!</i>

00:14:11.290 --> 00:14:14.490
<i>The only real reason why she's here is 
to provide me with this single moment.</i>

00:14:14.490 --> 00:14:16.170
Would you like some shiokara as a topping?

00:14:16.170 --> 00:14:17.010
It smells like seafood.

00:14:17.010 --> 00:14:17.790
No, thanks.

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:20.540
See you two later.

00:14:21.020 --> 00:14:21.540
Now, then...

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:24.250
Let's finish our work.

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:25.600
Cleaning, doing the laundry,

00:14:25.600 --> 00:14:27.870
making snacks, and getting ready for dinner.

00:14:27.870 --> 00:14:29.740
Leave the cleaning and laundry to me.

00:14:29.740 --> 00:14:33.930
Well, that's about the only thing
I could let you do, First Lieutenant.

00:14:34.710 --> 00:14:36.560
I'm not in the force anymore.

00:14:37.010 --> 00:14:38.130
Don't call me that.

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:40.060
That's what I'm used to calling you.

00:14:40.320 --> 00:14:41.420
Do you mind?

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:44.320
<i>What you're used to?</i>

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:47.880
Well, if you insist!

00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:50.820
However, you can still call me 
"Midorin" whenever you feel like it.

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:54.200
<i>It's just easier than calling 
you "Ukai-san," really.</i>

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:55.680
In any event, I'll get started 
on cleaning immediately—

00:14:55.680 --> 00:14:56.510
But!

00:14:58.140 --> 00:15:02.830
Cleaning Milady's room 
is my duty and my duty alone!

00:15:03.980 --> 00:15:07.020
I take Milady's hair that
has stuck to her pillow...

00:15:07.980 --> 00:15:09.870
Collect every single strand...

00:15:09.870 --> 00:15:12.720
And then someday, I'll add that hair 
to a doll that looks just like her,

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:14.890
and give it to her as a present!

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:16.530
<i>Milady.</i>

00:15:16.530 --> 00:15:17.270
<i>Hmm?</i>

00:15:18.390 --> 00:15:19.490
<i>Please take this.</i>

00:15:19.490 --> 00:15:20.100
<i>Huh?</i>

00:15:20.710 --> 00:15:23.480
<i>It's a doll using your own real hair.</i>

00:15:23.920 --> 00:15:26.520
<i>I made the clothing myself, of course.</i>

00:15:29.720 --> 00:15:32.780
<i>You made this by hand?</i>

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:33.780
<i>Yes.</i>

00:15:34.690 --> 00:15:35.880
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:39.100
<i>This is the most thoughtful 
present I've ever received.</i>

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:40.330
<i>Let's get married.</i>

00:15:41.400 --> 00:15:42.760
That'd be great!

00:15:42.760 --> 00:15:43.790
That's pretty disgusting.

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:44.800
What?!

00:15:44.800 --> 00:15:46.820
Calm down and think about it for a second.

00:15:46.820 --> 00:15:49.850
What if I secretly collected your hair

00:15:49.850 --> 00:15:52.930
and then gave you a doll that looked 
exactly like you as a present?

00:15:53.940 --> 00:15:56.470
I'd throw it on the ground immediately.

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:57.310
It'd be disgusting.

00:15:58.420 --> 00:16:00.060
What a wonderful reward.

00:16:00.440 --> 00:16:01.180
Maybe I should do it.

00:16:01.990 --> 00:16:06.230
You should take into account how 
much Milady cares for me.

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:10.840
I think that if you tried to quantify 
that value, it'd end up negative.

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:17.940
You wouldn't understand our bond.
You just got here a week ago.

00:16:17.940 --> 00:16:20.170
It's pretty obvious she tries to avoid you.

00:16:20.170 --> 00:16:21.500
That can't be true!

00:16:22.200 --> 00:16:25.840
Well, I'll at least take your 
opinion into consideration.

00:16:25.840 --> 00:16:28.790
Maybe I'll just keep the doll
I make of her to admire on my own.

00:16:28.790 --> 00:16:30.210
That's pretty creepy in its own right.

00:16:30.410 --> 00:16:34.870
I could dress it up with all sorts of 
frilly clothes she hasn't worn for me yet.

00:16:35.980 --> 00:16:37.600
Hey, Kamoi.

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:38.350
Yes?

00:16:41.010 --> 00:16:41.980
What do you think?

00:16:44.070 --> 00:16:45.730
What do you mean?

00:16:46.210 --> 00:16:50.330
These are the type of 
frilly clothes you like...

00:16:50.950 --> 00:16:56.360
You don't mean you completely changed 
your look to match what I'm into?

00:16:56.980 --> 00:16:58.540
Y-Yeah.

00:17:00.650 --> 00:17:03.870
It's so frustrating that you 
still just don't understand.

00:17:05.480 --> 00:17:06.370
Listen up.

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:11.120
What I like is pure, elegant, 
fleeting, and slightly sweet.

00:17:11.120 --> 00:17:13.440
Similar to a fairy.

00:17:13.440 --> 00:17:16.630
If you want to try to classify it,
 it'd be classical lolita.

00:17:17.100 --> 00:17:19.250
It doesn't matter how many frills you add,

00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:22.640
the black loli thing you have going on with 
your look is a complete antithesis to that.

00:17:24.220 --> 00:17:26.630
I had a feeling that'd be the case.

00:17:26.630 --> 00:17:30.070
But it just didn't look good on me at all.

00:17:31.170 --> 00:17:34.210
I-I can't wear this.

00:17:34.850 --> 00:17:37.450
I mean I'd love people talking 
behind my back about this, but...

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:41.100
If Kamoi doesn't like it, 
then there's no point.

00:17:44.180 --> 00:17:46.390
And then, after some trial and error,

00:17:46.390 --> 00:17:48.890
I ended up with this "black lolita" style,

00:17:48.890 --> 00:17:51.150
but I didn't know the first 
thing about makeup or whatever,

00:17:51.150 --> 00:17:52.890
so I got to learn about that,

00:17:52.890 --> 00:17:55.410
and figuring out my own way of 
doing things was pretty fun.

00:17:56.990 --> 00:18:01.290
I have you to thank for opening 
up a new world to me, Kamoi.

00:18:03.010 --> 00:18:04.850
I told you this before,

00:18:05.220 --> 00:18:09.420
but since you've already had your 
period, you're not even my type.

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:12.170
However,

00:18:13.230 --> 00:18:18.610
if you're having fun, then I think 
your clothes are happier for it.

00:18:20.610 --> 00:18:24.080
<i>She's rewarding that masochistic part 
of me by telling me I'm not her type,</i>

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:26.370
<i>but at the same time she's 
trying to make me feel better!</i>

00:18:27.250 --> 00:18:27.890
I love you.

00:18:27.890 --> 00:18:29.160
Well, I don't.

00:18:29.160 --> 00:18:30.490
I was rejected!

00:18:30.490 --> 00:18:33.000
You're really difficult to 
deal with, you know that?

00:18:34.240 --> 00:18:37.010
I heard this was the most important 
assignment we have in the afternoon,

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:40.970
but I didn't think it'd be walking the dog.

00:18:41.470 --> 00:18:43.780
Plus, I'm in this disguise...

00:18:45.660 --> 00:18:48.340
And what's up with you, Kamoi.

00:18:48.340 --> 00:18:50.100
Shh. Be quiet.

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:53.220
So you got another maid?

00:18:53.220 --> 00:18:53.940
There she is!

00:18:54.520 --> 00:18:57.070
Well, a maid that wants to 
put shiokara on bread.

00:18:57.070 --> 00:18:58.910
Sounds like a pretty fun maid.

00:18:58.910 --> 00:18:59.950
I see.

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:01.360
This was your true goal.

00:19:03.100 --> 00:19:05.930
Milady commonly 
sees through my disguises,

00:19:05.930 --> 00:19:09.000
but she has yet to see through this one.

00:19:09.800 --> 00:19:11.620
I'm wearing traditionally Japanese 
clothes, and covering up my muscles.

00:19:11.940 --> 00:19:17.210
Also, I can use this camera to candidly 
record Milady growing up.

00:19:18.560 --> 00:19:19.550
Illegal, however.

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:20.920
I'm just watching over her.

00:19:20.920 --> 00:19:23.380
It's better than the doll using her hair,

00:19:23.380 --> 00:19:25.870
but even with how much I like you,

00:19:25.870 --> 00:19:27.930
stalking her like this is kind of creepy.

00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:29.310
I'm just watching over her.

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:30.760
And then...

00:19:30.760 --> 00:19:33.160
Oh, it's a Samoyed!

00:19:33.160 --> 00:19:34.870
How cute!

00:19:34.870 --> 00:19:35.660
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:19:36.140 --> 00:19:37.800
First Lieutenant, you hide, just in case.

00:19:37.800 --> 00:19:39.280
R-Right.

00:19:41.090 --> 00:19:43.520
Your dog is cute.

00:19:43.520 --> 00:19:44.910
Could I pet it?

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:48.290
<i>S-She'll notice if I say something.</i>

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:49.820
What?

00:19:49.820 --> 00:19:51.850
Could I pet your...

00:19:51.850 --> 00:19:53.220
What?

00:19:53.950 --> 00:19:55.840
It's fine.

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:56.990
What?

00:19:58.620 --> 00:20:01.010
I guess she's hard of hearing.

00:20:01.010 --> 00:20:01.930
Too bad.

00:20:01.930 --> 00:20:04.500
The Samoyed looked all fluffy.

00:20:05.230 --> 00:20:07.100
<i>I got past that!</i>

00:20:07.100 --> 00:20:08.680
<i>She got through that hurdle.</i>

00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:11.660
<i>That's why she was dressed 
up as an old woman, huh?</i>

00:20:11.660 --> 00:20:12.940
<i>Kamoi's pretty good.</i>

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:15.440
<b>She didn't really 
think that far ahead</b>

00:20:15.790 --> 00:20:18.270
Anyway, Misha-chan, I'll see you tomorrow.

00:20:18.270 --> 00:20:20.230
Yeah, bye!

00:20:24.600 --> 00:20:26.950
Milady and Washizaki-sama 
have gone on their own ways.

00:20:27.360 --> 00:20:29.310
We have to get Gon home as fast as possible,

00:20:29.310 --> 00:20:30.830
and welcome Milady home.

00:20:31.280 --> 00:20:32.820
Go, Gon!

00:20:37.670 --> 00:20:39.850
What's up with that old lady?

00:20:39.850 --> 00:20:41.170
She's really fast!

00:20:41.170 --> 00:20:42.920
She's amazing!

00:20:45.600 --> 00:20:49.230
<i>An old lady running through a 
residential area with a large dog.</i>

00:20:49.230 --> 00:20:50.860
<i>That stands out quite a bit.</i>

00:20:52.010 --> 00:20:53.600
Good work today.

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:55.660
This is all of our work for now.

00:20:55.660 --> 00:20:59.020
It was fun getting to work 
with you after so long.

00:20:59.350 --> 00:21:00.950
I've fallen in love with you even more.

00:21:02.590 --> 00:21:05.030
That will only be for the
 remainder of the month.

00:21:05.440 --> 00:21:09.440
Wouldn't it be better for you use 
that time to find your next job?

00:21:09.440 --> 00:21:10.160
Yeah.

00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:14.790
Thinking about how this little honeymoon 
of ours is bound to come to an end...

00:21:16.010 --> 00:21:17.470
It gives me the chills!

00:21:17.470 --> 00:21:19.290
You just caught a cold.

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:22.550
You really cramp my style, you know that?

00:21:23.020 --> 00:21:25.340
Honestly, I have no clue how to handle you.

00:21:28.050 --> 00:21:29.230
You're letting me have a reward!

00:21:29.230 --> 00:21:30.310
What a pain.

00:21:31.310 --> 00:21:34.670
In the end, as long as I'm 
depending on that woman for food,

00:21:34.670 --> 00:21:37.440
I can't get rid of her.

00:21:40.600 --> 00:21:44.190
She's going to get more and 
more brazen at this rate!

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:46.920
<i>If I knew something that she didn't like</i>

00:21:46.920 --> 00:21:49.240
<i>then I might be able to come out on top.</i>

00:21:52.470 --> 00:21:55.000
<i>I doubt that even exists.</i>

00:21:55.520 --> 00:21:57.800
I'll be leaving now.

00:21:57.800 --> 00:21:58.520
See you later.

00:21:58.520 --> 00:21:59.580
Goodbye.

00:22:01.410 --> 00:22:02.250
See you tomorrow.

00:22:04.130 --> 00:22:05.640
Kamoi, see you tomorrow!

00:22:05.640 --> 00:22:07.300
I get it!　
